                pinchat-only: in test-preview mode the header names the bot
                being previewed (`displayName` resolves to `Test Bot <link>`
                there), so the preview is identifiable. `text-xs` is the
                caption level, so it reads as a subtitle rather than competing
                with the room name.
              -->
              <div
                v-if="isTestPreview"
                class="min-w-0 truncate text-xs text-content-subtle"
              >
                {{ displayName }}
              </div>
              <!--
                pinchat-only: the agent's online/offline line. The redesign
                dropped it, noting that where it should live was "a design
                decision, not a merge one" — this is that decision: under the
                room name, which is where pinchat had it and where the
                dashboard's own link preview still draws it. A guest is meant
                to know whether anyone is there before they type.

                The dot is `border` rather than a fill when away, so the two
                states differ in shape as well as colour (`color-not-only`).
                Colours come from tokens, so on a guest link they follow the
                header's `--color-content*` overrides — see chatHeaderStyle.ts.
              -->
              <div
                v-if="
                  presence.visible && agentPresenceEnabled && !isTestPreview
